Thu Sep 24 06:15:25 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 0.3.0 (breaking upstream rework):
  * Runner integrations, Advisor Gate and Composite routing,
    Auto presets, new Rust/Python embedding APIs, provider
    translation and tool-loop fixes
  * Drops the legacy Python server, the switchyard console
    script and its serve/launch commands: python-switchyard
    is now the importable library only, without console
    script or alternatives; the Recommends from the daemon
    goes away with the documented CLI workflow
  * Python runtime requirements drop to nothing (upstream
    dependencies = []); the license closure re-derived
    (224/233 crates, same seven identifiers)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Aug 17 08:22:45 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Initial package (version 0.2.0):
  * Rust proxy that routes LLM traffic across providers and
    translates between the OpenAI Chat, Anthropic Messages and
    OpenAI Responses wire formats.
  * Ships the daemon as switchyard-server together with a systemd
    service, a switchyard system user and /etc/switchyard for the
    required config.toml.
  * Ships upstream's nemo-switchyard Python distribution as
    python-switchyard: the switchyard command line client and the
    importable switchyard and switchyard_rust modules with their
    pyo3 extension, built with maturin.
